The latest 60 Minutes featured Norah O'Donnell's report on U.S. military failures at the outset of the war with Iran, in which the Tehran regime launched drone attacks on American bases, including one that struck an Army command post in Kuwait and killed six soldiers.

On Monday, Donald Trump went after the newsmagazine, writing on Truth Social, &#8220;The new people running 60 Minutes are even worse than their predecessors.&#8221;

Trump wrote, &#8220;A recent study on an attack in the early stages of Iran was not correctly stated. Since February 28, 2026, the start of Epic Fury, Iran has fired between 8,000-9,000 One-way Attack Drones. Only 2 of them got through, resulting in U.S. fatalities, both on the first day, hitting Kuwait and Saudi Arabia. Likewise, Iran has fired about 2,000 Ballistic Missiles. Only 1 out of the 2,0000 got through, and caused U.S. fatalities (Jordan). Translation: 99.99% of Iranian missiles and drones have been shot down or, in any event, not caused U.S. deaths. CENTCOM defensive measures have been historically effective. No one in the World has the ability to do so well. All of this being left out of the 60 Minutes &#8216;report.' Thank you for your attention to this matter.&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories News Willie Geist To Depart MS NOW's 'Morning Joe,' Will Expand NBC News Role And Continue To Host 'Sunday Today' Politics Bowen Yang Returns To 'Saturday Night Live' As Jensen Huang In Cold Open That Skewers Tech Billionaires' Susceptibility To Honey Pot Plots

But the 60 Minutes report, the result of an eight month investigation, included an interview with Major Stephen Ramsbottom, who filed a whistleblower complaint to Congress, calling for an investigation into why there was not adequate protection from attack drones. He said that at Port Shuaiba, an Army command post that is about 65 miles from Iran, there was &#8220;nothing there&#8221; to protect from an aerial attack. Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

&#8220;The site had no physician, no fixed aid station, and only one ambulance,&#8221; he said.

The segment also featured other interviews, including with family members of the victims, as well as satellite imagery that showed the scale of damage that had not previously been disclosed by the Pentagon. Among the family members featured was Joey Amor, whose wife, Master Sgt. Nicole Amor, was among the service members killed. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

CBS News has not yet commented on Trump's post.

The show underwent a shakeup in May, replacing its executive producer with Nick Bilton and three correspondents &#8212; Cecilia Vega, Sharyn Alfonsi and Scott Pelley &#8212; fired. They have made claims of CBS executive interference on stories, including ones that are critical of the Trump administration. The network has denied those claims and has said that they are part of the editorial process under editor in chief Bari Weiss.

Trump sued 60 Minutes in 2024 after it aired an interview with his rival in the presidential election, Kamala Harris. The lawsuit, over the way that Harris' interview was edited, was widely seen by legal experts as baseless, but the network, seeking the Trump administration approval for its sale to Skydance, settled the litigation.

After a long and thorough search, Amazon MGM Studios has found its next James Bond as Robert Pattinson has landed the coveted role in the next installment in the hit spy franchise. Following the last round of screen tests that Deadline first reported at the end of October, producers Amy Pascal and David Heyman and director Denis Villenueve landed on the Primetime star to lead the franchise for Amazon MGM Studios.

